## Purpose

This question evaluates practical accessibility implementation in SwiftUI, lightweight persistence strategies, and architectural awareness for beginner-level candidates.

## Key Concepts

- SwiftUI accessibility modifiers (`accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityHint`, `accessibilityValue`)
- Codable persistence to the app's Documents directory
- MVVM architecture with a minimal data model
- Dynamic Type support and color-contrast considerations (WCAG AA compliance)

## Code Example

```swift
struct Note: Codable, Identifiable {
    let id: UUID
    let title: String
    let tag: String  // e.g., "blue", "red", "green"
}

class NotesStore: ObservableObject {
    @Published var notes: [Note] = []

    private var documentsURL: URL {
        FileManager.default.urls(for: .documentDirectory, in: .userDomainMask)[0]
            .appendingPathComponent("notes.json")
    }

    init() { loadNotes() }

    func loadNotes() {
        guard let data = try? Data(contentsOf: documentsURL),
              let decoded = try? JSONDecoder().decode([Note].self, from: data) else { return }
        notes = decoded
    }

    func saveNotes() {
        guard let data = try? JSONEncoder().encode(notes) else { return }
        try? data.write(to: documentsURL)
    }
}

struct NoteRow: View {
    let note: Note

    var body: some View {
        HStack {
            VStack(alignment: .leading) {
                Text(note.title)
                    .font(.body)
                    .dynamicTypeSize(...(.accessibility3))

                Text(note.tag.capitalized)
                    .font(.caption)
                    .padding(.horizontal, 8)
                    .padding(.vertical, 4)
                    .background(tagColor(note.tag))
                    .foregroundColor(tagTextColor(note.tag))
                    .clipShape(Capsule())
            }
            Spacer()
        }
        .padding(.vertical, 8)
        .accessibilityElement(children: .combine)
        .accessibilityLabel("\(note.title), tagged \(note.tag)")
        .accessibilityHint("Double tap to open this note")
    }

    private func tagColor(_ tag: String) -> Color {
        switch tag.lowercased() {
        case "blue":   return Color(red: 0.0, green: 0.48, blue: 1.0)
        case "green":  return Color(red: 0.18, green: 0.8, blue: 0.25)
        case "red":    return Color(red: 0.9, green: 0.2, blue: 0.2)
        default:       return .gray
        }
    }

    private func tagTextColor(_ tag: String) -> Color {
        return .white  // High contrast against all tag colors
    }
}

struct ContentView: View {
    @StateObject private var store = NotesStore()

    var body: some View {
        NavigationStack {
            List(store.notes) { note in
                NoteRow(note: note)
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Test Plan

1. **Accessibility Audit**: Verify VoiceOver reads labels and hints correctly for each row
2. **Dynamic Type**: Test with largest accessibility sizes to confirm layout remains usable
3. **Contrast Validation**: Use accessibility inspector or contrast checker to verify WCAG AA compliance (4.5:1 ratio)
4. **Persistence**: Confirm notes survive app restart by adding a note, killing the app, and relaunching
5. **Unit Tests**: Test `Note` Codable encoding/decoding and `NotesStore` save/load roundtrip

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates advanced iOS system design skills: offline-first architecture, end-to-end encryption with per-channel keys, deterministic state reconstruction via journal replay, and secure CloudKit sync. It tests proficiency with CryptoKit, Core Data/SQLite, and SwiftUI while assessing understanding of security principles and crash resilience.

## Key Concepts
- **Append-only journaling**: Immutable log of all state mutations enabling deterministic replay
- **Per-channel key management**: Unique symmetric keys per channel stored in Keychain with rotation support
- **Deterministic replay**: Reconstruct app state by replaying journal operations in order
- **End-to-end encryption**: Notes encrypted on-device with ChaChaPoly; CloudKit stores only ciphertext
- **CloudKit sync**: Encrypted payloads sync when online; keys never leave the device

## Data Models
```swift
struct Channel {
    let id: UUID
    var name: String
    var encryptionKeyRef: String // Keychain reference
    var lastKeyRotation: Date
}

struct SecureNote {
    let id: UUID
    let channelId: UUID
    var encryptedContent: Data // ChaChaPoly sealed box
    var encryptedContentHash: String
    var createdAt: Date
    var modifiedAt: Date
}

struct JournalEntry: Identifiable {
    let id: UUID
    let timestamp: Date
    let operation: JournalOperation // .create, .update, .delete
    let entityType: String // "note", "channel"
    let entityId: UUID
    let payloadHash: String // SHA256 of encrypted data
}
```

## Encryption Scheme
1. **Key Generation**: Generate 256-bit symmetric keys via CryptoKit SymmetricKey
2. **Storage**: Store keys in Keychain with kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly
3. **Encryption**: Use ChaChaPoly.seal() with channel key to encrypt note content
4. **Rotation**: Generate new key, re-encrypt all channel notes, update Keychain reference

## Minimal UI Sketch (SwiftUI)
```swift
struct SecureNotesView: View {
    @StateObject private var vm = NotesViewModel()
    @State private var showingCompose = false

    var body: some View {
        NavigationStack {
            List(vm.notes) { note in
                NoteRow(note: note)
            }
            .searchable(text: $vm.searchText)
            .toolbar {
                Button("+") { showingCompose = true }
            }
            .sheet(isPresented: $showingCompose) {
                ComposeNoteView(channelId: vm.selectedChannel)
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Test Plan
- **Replay Correctness**: Create operations, clear state, replay journal, verify identical state
- **Security Tests**: Verify key isolation, confirm ciphertext only, test key rotation integrity
- **Sync Tests**: Offline mutations sync correctly when online, conflict resolution works
- **Crash Resilience**: Force kill mid-write, verify journal integrity on restart

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates your ability to translate a data-driven schema into a production-ready iOS application with offline resilience, dynamic UI generation, and enterprise-grade networking patterns.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic SwiftUI UI generation from JSON schema definitions
- Reactive state management with Combine for live validation
- Offline-first architecture using Core Data with conflict resolution
- Idempotent REST operations with exponential backoff retry logic
- Field-level dependency management for conditional visibility

## Code Example

```swift
struct FieldDefinition: Codable {
    let id: String
    let type: FieldType
    let label: String
    let validation: ValidationRules?
    let visibility: VisibilityRules?
    let dependencies: [String]?
}

enum FieldType: String, Codable {
    case text, email, number, date, picker, toggle
}

struct ValidationRules: Codable {
    let required: Bool?
    let minLength: Int?
    let maxLength: Int?
    let pattern: String?
    let customRules: [String]?
}

class DynamicFormEngine: ObservableObject {
    @Published var formState: [String: Any]
    @Published var validationErrors: [String: String]
    @Published var visibleFields: Set<String>

    private let schema: FormSchema
    private let persistenceManager: CoreDataManager
    private let networkManager: NetworkManager

    init(schema: FormSchema) {
        self.schema = schema
        self.formState = [:]
        self.validationErrors = [:]
        self.visibleFields = Set(schema.fields.map { $0.id })
        self.persistenceManager = CoreDataManager()
        self.networkManager = NetworkManager()

        setupFieldDependencies()
        loadOfflineData()
    }

    func updateValue(for fieldId: String, value: Any) {
        formState[fieldId] = value
        validateField(fieldId)
        updateFieldVisibility()
        saveOffline()
    }

    private func validateField(_ fieldId: String) {
        guard let field = schema.fields.first(where: { $0.id == fieldId }),
              let validation = field.validation else {
            validationErrors.removeValue(forKey: fieldId)
            return
        }

        let value = formState[fieldId]
        var errors: [String] = []

        if validation.required == true && (value == nil || value as? String == "") {
            errors.append("This field is required")
        }

        if let stringValue = value as? String {
            if let minLength = validation.minLength, stringValue.count < minLength {
                errors.append("Minimum length is \(minLength) characters")
            }

            if let maxLength = validation.maxLength, stringValue.count > maxLength {
                errors.append("Maximum length is \(maxLength) characters")
            }

            if let pattern = validation.pattern {
                let regex = try? NSRegularExpression(pattern: pattern)
                let range = NSRange(location: 0, length: stringValue.utf16.count)
                if regex?.firstMatch(in: stringValue, options: [], range: range) == nil {
                    errors.append("Invalid format")
                }
            }
        }

        validationErrors[fieldId] = errors.isEmpty ? nil : errors.first
    }

    private func updateFieldVisibility() {
        var newVisibleFields = Set<String>()

        for field in schema.fields {
            if let visibility = field.visibility {
                if shouldShowField(field: field, rules: visibility) {
                    newVisibleFields.insert(field.id)
                }
            } else {
                newVisibleFields.insert(field.id)
            }
        }

        visibleFields = newVisibleFields
    }

    private func shouldShowField(field: FieldDefinition, rules: VisibilityRules) -> Bool {
        guard let conditions = rules.conditions else { return true }

        for condition in conditions {
            let dependentValue = formState[condition.fieldId]
            let expectedValue = condition.value

            switch condition.operator {
            case .equals:
                if "\(dependentValue ?? "")" != "\(expectedValue)" {
                    return false
                }
            case .notEquals:
                if "\(dependentValue ?? "")" == "\(expectedValue)" {
                    return false
                }
            case .contains:
                if let stringValue = dependentValue as? String {
                    if !stringValue.contains(expectedValue) {
                        return false
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        return true
    }

    func submitForm() async throws {
        let submissionData = FormSubmission(
            id: UUID().uuidString,
            timestamp: Date(),
            formData: formState,
            schemaVersion: schema.version
        )

        try await networkManager.submitForm(submissionData)
        persistenceManager.markAsSubmitted(submissionData.id)
    }
}

class CoreDataManager {
    func saveOffline(_ data: FormSubmission) {
        let context = persistentContainer.viewContext
        let entity = FormSubmissionEntity(context: context)
        entity.id = data.id
        entity.timestamp = data.timestamp
        entity.formData = try? JSONEncoder().encode(data.formData)
        entity.isSubmitted = false

        try? context.save()
    }

    func getPendingSubmissions() -> [FormSubmission] {
        let context = persistentContainer.viewContext
        let request: NSFetchRequest<FormSubmissionEntity> = FormSubmissionEntity.fetchRequest()
        request.predicate = NSPredicate(format: "isSubmitted == false")

        return (try? context.fetch(request))?.compactMap { entity in
            guard let data = entity.formData,
                  let formData = try? JSONDecoder().decode([String: Any].self, from: data) else {
                return nil
            }

            return FormSubmission(
                id: entity.id ?? "",
                timestamp: entity.timestamp ?? Date(),
                formData: formData,
                schemaVersion: "1.0"
            )
        } ?? []
    }
}

class NetworkManager {
    func submitForm(_ data: FormSubmission) async throws {
        let url = URL(string: "https://api.example.com/forms")!
        var request = URLRequest(url: url)
        request.httpMethod = "POST"
        request.setValue("application/json", forHTTPHeaderField: "Content-Type")
        request.setValue(data.id, forHTTPHeaderField: "X-Idempotency-Key")

        let jsonData = try JSONEncoder().encode(data)
        request.httpBody = jsonData

        try await executeWithRetry(request: request)
    }

    private func executeWithRetry(request: URLRequest, maxRetries: Int = 3) async throws {
        var delay: TimeInterval = 1.0

        for attempt in 0...maxRetries {
            do {
                let (_, response) = try await URLSession.shared.data(for: request)

                if let httpResponse = response as? HTTPURLResponse {
                    if httpResponse.statusCode == 200 || httpResponse.statusCode == 201 {
                        return
                    } else if httpResponse.statusCode == 409 {
                        return
                    } else if httpResponse.statusCode >= 500 {
                        throw NetworkError.serverError
                    } else {
                        throw NetworkError.clientError(httpResponse.statusCode)
                    }
                }
            } catch {
                if attempt == maxRetries {
                    throw error
                }

                try await Task.sleep(nanoseconds: UInt64(delay * 1_000_000_000))
                delay *= 2
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Architecture Benefits

- **Schema-driven**: UI adapts automatically to schema changes without code modifications
- **Offline-first**: Core Data ensures data persistence and sync when connectivity restores
- **Reactive validation**: Combine framework provides real-time feedback as users type
- **Idempotent operations**: Retry logic prevents duplicate submissions during network issues
- **Conditional rendering**: Complex field dependencies handled through declarative rules

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates offline-first routing with on-device compute, real-time edge-weight updates, crash safety, and cryptographic authenticity. It also tests SwiftUI/Combine integration and mobile performance optimization.

## Key Concepts
- **Graph algorithms**: A* with incremental weight updates
- **Offline-first data store**: SQLite with write-ahead logging for durability
- **Streaming ingestion**: Combine for processing traffic events
- **Crash safety**: Checkpoints and state persistence for reliable resume
- **Cryptographic verification**: CryptoKit for signed map updates
- **SwiftUI dashboard**: Route visualization with ETA and confidence metrics

## Code Example
```swift
// Graph structure
struct Node: Hashable { let id: String; let coordinate: CLLocationCoordinate2D }
struct Edge { let from: Node.ID; let to: Node.ID; var weight: Double }

class RoutingEngine: ObservableObject {
    @Published var currentRoute: [Node] = []
    @Published var eta: TimeInterval = 0
    @Published var confidence: Double = 0

    private var graph: AdjacencyList<Node.ID, Edge>
    private var checkpoint: RouteCheckpoint?

    // MARK: - A* with Checkpoint Resume
    func computeRoute(from start: Node.ID, to end: Node.ID) {
        let checkpoint = RouteCheckpoint(currentNode: start)
        currentRoute = aStar(graph: graph, start: start, goal: end, checkpoint: checkpoint)
        self.checkpoint = checkpoint
        updateETA()
    }

    func invalidateEdges(_ edges: [Edge.ID]) {
        guard let cp = checkpoint else { return }
        currentRoute = aStar(graph: graph, start: cp.currentNode, goal: goal, checkpoint: cp)
        updateConfidence()
    }

    // MARK: - Combine Traffic Ingestion
    private var cancellables = Set<AnyCancellable>()

    func subscribe(to publisher: AnyPublisher<TrafficEvent, Never>) {
        publisher
            .filter { $0.isSignificant }
            .sink { [weak self] event in
                self?.applyTrafficEvent(event)
            }
            .store(in: &cancellables)
    }

    private func applyTrafficEvent(_ event: TrafficEvent) {
        graph.updateWeight(edgeId: event.edgeId, weight: event.delay)
        invalidateEdges([event.edgeId])
    }

    // MARK: - Map Update Verification
    func verifyAndApplyMapUpdate(_ update: MapUpdate) throws {
        try CryptoKit.verify(update.signature, for: update.data)
        try applyMapUpdate(update)
        checkpoint = nil // Invalidate checkpoint after structural changes
    }
}
```

## Test Plan

| Category | Test Case | Method |
|----------|-----------|--------|
| Routing | A* finds optimal path on static graph | XCTest with known graph |
| Routing | Returns to checkpoint on weight update | Mock weight change, verify partial recomputation |
| Streaming | Traffic events update weights correctly | Combine test publisher, assert graph state |
| Offline | Route computed without network | Disable network, run computeRoute |
| Crash Safety | Resume from checkpoint after simulated crash | Inject crash state, verify recovery |
| Crypto | Reject tampered map updates | Modify signature, expect CryptoKit error |
| UI | Dashboard reflects route/ETA/confidence | ViewInspector snapshot tests |

